# MiMo-V2.6-Pro (Xiaomi, 2026): a 1T MoE of 70 layers, most of them sliding-window
# attention with a 128-token window and a learned sink per head. A global layer comes
# every 7 or 8 layers, and the first layer is global and dense.
#
# Query and key heads are 192 wide and value heads 128; a third of each query and key
# head is rotated, with a long RoPE base on global layers only. Three MTP layers,
# sliding-window and dense, each read the main model's final hidden state and predict
# 1 to 3 tokens further ahead. Vision and audio encoders are not described here.
d_model    = 6144
vocab_size = 152576

norm    = rmsnorm(eps=1e-5)
attn    = gqa(num_heads=128, num_kv_heads=8, head_dim=192, v_head_dim=128,
              fused_qkv=true, rope=rope(base=10000000, fraction=0.334))
local   = attn(sliding_window_size=128, sinks=true, rope.base=10000)
dense   = gated_mlp(intermediate_size=16384, activation=swish)
experts = moe(num_experts=384, top_k=8, router=sigmoid, load_balancing=aux_free,
              aux_loss_coef=1e-5, aux_loss_scope=sequence,
              expert=gated_mlp(intermediate_size=2048, activation=swish))

# The values are scaled by 0.612, about sqrt(d_model / (128 heads * 128)). Scaling the
# output instead is the same, since its projection has no bias.
layer(mixer, ffn=experts) = [norm (mixer * 0.612)] [norm ffn]
F = layer(attn, dense)
G = layer(attn)
S = layer(local)

shared out = head
mtp = $h nextn(norm=norm) layer(local, dense) norm out

model = embed "F" "SSSSSS" "GSSSSSSS"^6 "GSSSSSS"^2 "G" norm @h out mtp^3
